+## Read-only reproduction
+
+Run from the WSmart-Route project root in an environment with the table
+script's dependencies. The existing review environment used for this check is
+`~/.cache/wsr-main-venv/bin/python`; dependency installation and simulation
+execution are not part of these commands.
+
+```bash
+OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 ~/.cache/wsr-main-venv/bin/python .agent/cache/tools/codex_paper_audit_20260926.py
+OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 ~/.cache/wsr-main-venv/bin/python .agent/cache/tools/codex_late_rows_review_20260927.py
+OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 ~/.cache/wsr-main-venv/bin/python logic/gen/gen_paper_latex.py --tables-only --tables-dir ~/.cache/wsr-review/codex-paper-p10-audit/Tables --figures-dir ~/.cache/wsr-review/codex-paper-p10-audit/Figures
+```
+
+The first script writes `audit.json`, `trip_counts.json`, `cf_mirrors.csv`,
+`timing.csv`, and `90d_not_on_30d_front.csv` beneath
+`~/.cache/wsr-review/codex-paper-audit/`. The second writes
+`.agent/cache/codex_late_rows_review_20260927.json`. Its four-bin witness is
+unrelated to the P10 benchmark caveats; the updated paper example is separate.
+Neither command runs a policy or simulator. Preserve the input summaries/logs
+before any future corrected run replaces output files.
+
+The table reproduction compares numerical content. Template comments and
+exclusion-footnote wording may differ across revisions; do not treat those as
+changed experimental measurements. P10 changes only the horizon-table footnote, regenerated from the companion
+`logic/gen/json/paper_latex_config.json` patch; numerical cells and images are
+unchanged. Apply that companion patch before running the table-generation
+command above, so regeneration preserves the corrected footnote.
+
+## Deferred verification
+
+Recover the historical source/dependency revisions, resolved per-run configs,
+selection manifest, saved demand datasets and 90-day raw logs. Then determine
+which paths actually ran, validate route feasibility and timing scope, and
+choose affected comparisons for reruns. No new optimality, repeatability or
+capacity-feasibility certificate is asserted for the archived results.
