+\subsection{Implementation Provenance}\label{sec:provenance}
+
+The following checks distinguish archived observations from results that a
+corrected implementation might produce. Their file-level evidence and
+reproduction commands are recorded with the paper source.\footnote{See
+\path{Evidence/P10-provenance.md}, which maps each check below to the
+project's summary CSVs, archived logs/configurations, code revisions and
+read-only audit scripts.}
+The original executable revisions, resolved run settings and 90-day raw
+logs are pending recovery of the run records. Decisions on retaining or
+rerunning affected comparisons are deferred until those records are
+available; no corrected-run outcomes are substituted here.
+
+\paragraph{Archive and selection checks.}
+All 480 rows of the 30-day summary match the available raw logs on the ten
+recorded summary metrics. The six tables reproduce numerically from the
+summary CSVs, but the 90-day raw logs were not available for this check.
+The scenario-specific raw 30-day fronts contain 33 configurations, of
+which 23 occur in the 90-day archive. This accounts for the 151 off-front
+follow-ups noted above without reconstructing the original selection
+manifest. The later CF90-to-CF70 selector-mirroring defect likewise does
+not establish exact duplication in these archived outputs: none of the
+12 CF70/CF90 log pairs for either PSOMA or SANS has identical daily
+collected mass, collection count and overflow count. Historical parameter
+resolution remains to be checked; absence of duplicate outputs is not a
+proof that every parameter was applied correctly.
+
+\paragraph{Timing and randomness.}
+For all 480 archived 30-day samples, stored sample time differs from the
+sum of stored daily times, by approximately 1.93--89.86\,s. The old daily
+clock covered construction rather than the revised full policy, so summing
+it cannot recover the new timing definition. Timing columns and rankings
+here retain the archived clock. Fast-TSP's unseeded stochastic search and
+the former elapsed-time signal in ACO-HH limit seed-based repeatability.
+PSOMA formerly used global NumPy state, but the simulator explicitly
+reseeded that state per policy and day; the standalone solver's incomplete
+local-seed control is therefore not evidence that the archived simulator
+runs lacked seeding. Subsequent changes to the policy seed key can change
+future reruns even when the supplied simulation seed is unchanged.
+
+\paragraph{Solver-version exposure.}
+All 36 available 30-day pruned configurations enable BPC strong branching,
+a path subsequently identified as capable of returning suboptimal plans.
+Corrections to pricing, bounds and branching mean its archived comparisons
+cannot certify the revised solver. HGS exposure is more conditional: the
+corrected defect concerns limited-fleet splitting. The saved configuration
+sets no simulation fleet cap but does not record the HGS-specific
+\texttt{max\_vehicles} parameter; its historical resolution must be checked
+before declaring that path exposed or excluding HGS results on that basis.
+ACO-HH's pre-correction capacity relaxation could return an over-capacity
+incumbent, and the reviewed pre-correction implementation used all eleven registered
+operators despite the saved subset setting. These findings motivate
+historical path and route-feasibility checks; they do not by themselves
+prove which archived routes were infeasible. The revised simulator splits
+non-CTOP routes at capacity and records per-trip loads. That safeguard
+applies to future runs; the archived runs executed routes as returned.
+
+\paragraph{Scope of the comparisons.}
+The 224 integrity-filtered improver pairs remain descriptive comparisons
+of complete policy configurations, with neither identical input plans nor
+repeated independent stochastic trials established. Neither summary CSV
+contains a neural-constructor row. Neural-only adapter or Attention Model
+defects therefore do not require recalculation of these eight-constructor
+benchmark tables. These scope limits, together with the pending provenance
+checks, also apply to the interpretation of the results below.
 
